speechtext:
It empowers the governor in council on the advice of the commission to:
(a) prescribe standards of quality for any commodity in accordance with the terms of a report made pursuant to the provisions of this act and prescribe the manner in which such commodity shall be sold, offered for sale, or displayed for sale, and if such commodity is sold in packages or containers, the size, kind, and marking, branding or labelling of such packages or containers;
The goods must be in accordance with the grades and standards that have been established. There are of course some commodities covered under existing legislation, as already mentioned, for instance under the Food and Drugs Act or the Meat and Canned Foods Aet. Those already provided for would not, I assume, come under this bill.
